The national debt just crossed $40 trillion, the Fed raised rates for the first time since 2023, and the 10-year Treasury is sitting above 5%. Meanwhile the venture headlines look like a party — a record quarter with 83.6% of rounds pricing up. So is it a boom, or the bill coming due? This week Josh and Mike break down what expensive money actually means for founders and angels raising in Q4 2026: bridge vs. priced rounds, when venture debt is a runway extender and when it's a floating-rate trap, how angels re-price risk the Monday after a hike, how to spot a “dirty” up round hiding a down round in the terms, and the new rules for runway, pricing power, and hiring math in a hiking cycle. Money got expensive — the business world is heating up!

